@startuml enemy_ai_state_machine
' Super Mario Plus - enemy and boss AI transitions
' Verified against the source tree at commit b378acb.
' Matches: include/entity/IMobState.h, src/entity/EnemyStates/, src/entity/BossStates/

title Enemy and Boss AI — seven enemy states, nine boss states

state "Boss only" as BossOnly {
  [*] --> Intro
  Intro --> BossIdle : cutscene finished
  state "DebugInput" as Debug
  BossIdle --> Debug : debug build only
  Debug --> BossIdle
}

[*] --> Patrol : enemies start here

Patrol --> Idle : patrol distance reached
Idle --> Patrol : patrol timer elapsed

Patrol --> Run : player entered detection range
Idle   --> Run : player entered detection range
Run    --> Patrol : player left detection range

Run    --> Attack : player within attack range
Attack --> Run    : attack finished, still pursuing
Run    --> Skill  : a special move is off cooldown
Skill  --> Run    : skill finished

Attack --> Hurt : took damage
Run    --> Hurt : took damage
Patrol --> Hurt : took damage
Hurt   --> Run  : recovery elapsed

Hurt   --> Die : health reached zero
Die    --> [*] : removed; identifier recorded as defeated

BossIdle --> Run : player entered detection range

note right of Patrol
  Enemies flagged avoidCliffsAndWater
  turn back at ledges and at the edge
  of water, lava and poison. The check
  lives in the physics hook onHitWall,
  not in the AI.
end note

note bottom
  Base interface: IMobState
    enter(Mob&) / decideAction(Mob&) / process(Mob&) / exit(Mob&)
    onHitWall(Mob&, bool rightWall, bool isCliff)

  Enemy states (7): Idle, Patrol, Run, Attack, Skill, Hurt, Die
  Boss states  (9): the above plus Intro and DebugInput

  Unlike PlayerState, IMobState stores no back-reference;
  the Mob is passed as a parameter on every call.
end note

@enduml
